\f2\fs57\fsmilli28800 \cf2 \cb3 \ul \ulc2 Course Description/Purpose
\f1 \cb1 \ulnone \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf2 \cb3 This course introduces students without prior programming experience to the core programming concepts and software development practices for data-intensive applications in industry and government. Handling data and being able to investigate it and answer quantitative questions meaningfully is a critical skill, and programming should be one tool in your toolbox for gaining that ability. This course aims to develop the programming skills that enable you to engage in meaningful conversations with peers, coworkers, and collaborators about technical work, contribute to a data-oriented software development team, and perform data analysis and file manipulation tasks. The course will prepare students with the requisite programming skills that support further study and skill development in data science practice.
\f1 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs57\fsmilli28800 \cf2 \cb3 \ul \ulc2 Educational Objectives
\f1 \cb1 \ulnone \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf2 \cb3 After this course, students will be comfortable with the following skills:
\f1 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Use appropriate data structures like lists, dictionaries, and multidimensional arrays.
\f1 \cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Coding to perform data cleaning tasks and answer statistical questions about datasets.
\f1 \cb1 \
